 "final_text": "Submitted. Here's the leverage picture for the brief:\n\n**Long-term debt vs. equity, 3-year picture** (SEC 10-K data, CIK 0000018230):\n\n| FY | LT debt (noncurrent) | Equity* | LT Debt/Equity |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2022 | $25,714M | $15,891M | 1.62x |\n| 2023 | $24,472M | $19,503M | 1.25x |\n| 2024 | $27,351M | $19,494M | 1.40x |\n\n**3-yr average LT Debt/Equity: 1.43x**\n\n*One caveat worth flagging to Robin: the equity figure is `StockholdersEquityIncludingPortionAttributableToNoncontrollingInterest` \u2014 the parent-only equity concept wasn't available in the data source, so this includes a small noncontrolling-interest slice. Directionally it won't move the ratio meaningfully, but worth a footnote in the deck.\n\n**Internal AR relationship: none.** Checked both Books (customer/invoice tables, balance and aged-receivables reports, full transaction history) and the ERP customer master (1,007 active customers) for \"Caterpillar,\" \"Caterpillar Inc,\" and \"CAT\" \u2014 zero matches anywhere. We don't currently trade with them, independently double-checked.\n\nAll four fields recorded via `submit_answer`.",
